+## OpenStorm .184 typed translation key navigation
+
+Typed translator and contract calls contribute lazy translation key spans for
+navigation, hover, usages and diagnostics. Public instance methods and every
+non-null union alternative must prove their translation role. Foreign, scalar,
+unknown or missing-method receivers contribute no translation spans. Named keys,
+null-safe calls and dirty dependency invalidation use existing shared paths.
+
+Cross-file typed receiver, member, body and closure passes isolate address/offset
+variable memos and restore their caller's state, including after unwinding.
+Equal-sized temporary parser buffers cannot exchange inferred receiver types.
+
